# Lite free features stay open in the full app

Lite is the free surface. Anything a Lite user can open or use without signing in must stay available in the full app.

## Do

- Before adding a lock (login gate, `ynow-menu-lock`, `ynow-full-only` hide, auth redirect, or a paid-only flag), check whether Lite still shows that tab, control, or result.
- If the full app must lock it and Lite still leaves it open, **stop and tell the user** in the same turn: name the Lite path that remains free, and do not ship the lock until they confirm.
- Keep the two surfaces consistent: a Lite-free feature is either open in both, or the user has explicitly accepted that Lite stays open while the full app is locked.

## Do not

- Hide or gate a feature in the full app that Lite still renders (`body.ynow-lite`, `ynow-lite-only`, or an unlocked sidebar item).
- Treat “full app” as the stricter product by default. Lite-free is the floor.
